{"name":"Fundy Bay","hex":"#cdd2c9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Fundy Bay","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Alternative form of Bay of Fundy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Fundy_Bay"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bay of Fundy","blocks":[{"text":"The Bay of Fundy is a bay between the Canadian provinces of New Brunswick and Nova Scotia, with a small portion touching the U.S. state of Maine. It is an arm of the Gulf of Maine and part of the Atlantic Ocean. It has the highest tidal range in the world, averaging about 16 metres (52 ft) due to tidal resonance in its funnel-shaped basin. In one half-day tidal cycle, around 100 billion tonnes of water flows in and out, twice the combined flow of all the world's rivers."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/74/Wpdms_nasa_topo_bay_of_fundy_-_en.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay_of_Fundy","wikidata":"Q181857"},{"title":"Bay","blocks":[{"text":"A bay is a recessed, coastal body of water that directly connects to a larger main body of water, such as an ocean, a lake, or another bay. A large bay is usually called a gulf, sea, sound, or bight. A cove is a small, circular bay with a narrow entrance. A fjord is an elongated bay formed by glacial action.\nThe term embayment is also used for related features, such as extinct bays or freshwater environments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg/330px-Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay","wikidata":"Q39594"},{"title":"Bay (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Bay is a hair coat color of horses, characterized by a reddish-brown or brown body color with a black point coloration on the mane, tail, ear edges, and lower legs. Bay is one of the most common coat colors in many horse breeds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/BayMare.jpg/330px-BayMare.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay_(horse)","wikidata":"Q900906"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Bay_of_Fundy_High_Tide.jpg/250px-Bay_of_Fundy_High_Tide.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/76/Bay_of_Fundy_High_Tide.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Bay_of_Fundy_High_Tide.jpg/250px-Bay_of_Fundy_High_Tide.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABay_of_Fundy_High_Tide.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Bay_of_Fundy_Low_Tide.jpg/250px-Bay_of_Fundy_Low_Tide.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/cf/Bay_of_Fundy_Low_Tide.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Bay_of_Fundy_Low_Tide.jpg/250px-Bay_of_Fundy_Low_Tide.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABay_of_Fundy_Low_Tide.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/North_Atlantic_right_whale.jpg/500px-North_Atlantic_right_whale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/North_Atlantic_right_whale.jpg/1